let __v_147 = Value::from("Paracetamol is the one to take for a headache in pregnancy, at the lowest dose that works and for the shortest time - not ibuprofen or aspirin unless a doctor or midwife has told you to. Water, food and sleep do a lot, and a skipped meal, dehydration and caffeine withdrawal are the usual causes. Mention headaches that keep coming back to your midwife, and go in the same day if a bad headache comes with blurred vision or flashing lights, pain under the ribs, swelling of the face or hands, or vomiting after 20 weeks: that combination is the one that has to be checked for pre-eclampsia.");
