let __v_7251 = Value::from("An abnormal result is usually a number a little outside the range, not a diagnosis: a slightly low vitamin D, or a liver figure up after a bug, is repeated in a few weeks and settles. Ask three things on the phone - which test it was, what your number was and what the normal range is - and then what the plan is. \"They want to see you again\" usually means a value worth a look rather than bad news, and you can ask for a copy of the result.");
frame.store("ABNORMAL_RESULT_TEXT", __v_7251.clone())?;
let __v_7252 = Value::from("Yes - ring the surgery and ask the receptionist whether the result is back and whether anything needs doing, rather than waiting for a letter, and ask for a copy if you want one. If it is past the wait they promised, say when the sample was taken and ask who is going to look at it.");
frame.store("CHASE_RESULT_TEXT", __v_7252.clone())?;
let __v_7253 = Value::from("That is good news, and there is nothing to do about it: a clear result means nothing was found. Keep the letter or save the message, and if the symptom that started it off is still there in a few weeks, tell the GP even with a clear result behind you.");
frame.store("CLEAR_RESULT_TEXT", __v_7253.clone())?;
let __v_7254 = Value::from("That is the result you wanted: nothing found means there was nothing to treat, so the visit did its job. Keep the note the vet gave you, and if the same thing comes back, ring them rather than waiting to see whether it settles on its own.");
frame.store("CLEAR_RESULT_FOR_A_PET_TEXT", __v_7254.clone())?;
let __v_7255 = Value::from("Ask the vet to say what the result was and what the next step is, in those words. Most results a little outside the range are repeated in a few weeks rather than treated now, and it is worth knowing which one this is before you read the worst into it.");
frame.store("ABNORMAL_RESULT_FOR_A_PET_TEXT", __v_7255.clone())?;
let __v_7256 = Value::from("A negative result means the thing they were looking for was not found, which is usually the news you want: nothing to act on. If you were expecting it to show something, ring and ask what it means for you rather than reading it either way.");
frame.store("NEGATIVE_RESULT_TEXT", __v_7256.clone())?;
let __v_7257 = Value::from("Yes - nothing was found, so nothing is waiting on it. Build back up over a week or two rather than straight back to where you were, and ease off again if the symptom comes back.");
frame.store("AFTER_A_CLEAR_RESULT_EXERCISE", __v_7257.clone())?;
let __v_7258 = Value::from("Don't stop them on the strength of a clear result: ring whoever prescribed them and ask, because a test clearing one thing does not mean the medicine has done its job. A clear result answers the test, it does not end a prescription.");
frame.store("AFTER_A_CLEAR_RESULT_MEDICINE", __v_7258.clone())?;
let __v_7259 = Value::from("Nothing in the result keeps you off - but if you were signed off, whoever signed you off is the one who says it can end early, so ask them before you go back.");
frame.store("AFTER_A_CLEAR_RESULT_WORK", __v_7259.clone())?;
let __v_7260 = Value::from("Nothing in a clear result stops you driving. If the test was for a licence or an insurance medical, whoever asked for it decides, not the result on its own.");
frame.store("AFTER_A_CLEAR_RESULT_DRIVING", __v_7260.clone())?;
let __v_7261 = Value::from("Yes - nothing was found, so nothing in that result is holding you up. If it is a medicine or a note from work, ask whoever prescribed or signed it before you change anything: a clear result answers the test.");
frame.store("AFTER_A_CLEAR_RESULT_TEXT", __v_7261.clone())?;
