let __v_7367 = Value::from("A blood test is a small needle in the arm and a vial or two, about five minutes in the chair, and it checks red and white cells and platelets, kidney and liver figures, thyroid, cholesterol, vitamin D and blood sugar. It shows how the organs are working and whether something is short or high, which is what the GP reads against your symptoms, so ask what your number was and what the normal range is. You do not need to fast unless the surgery says so.");
frame.store("_A_BLOOD_TEST_TEXT", __v_7367.clone())?;
let __v_7368 = Value::from("Eight to twelve hours without food is the usual ask, and water is fine: book the first appointment of the morning, and tea or coffee with no milk still counts as fasting. Only some tests need it - a fasting cholesterol or a glucose, not a full blood count or a thyroid check - so read the letter, because eating by mistake usually means going back another day. Take your medicine as normal unless the letter says to skip it, and if you are diabetic ask the surgery how they want that morning to work.");
frame.store("_A_FASTING_BEFORE_A_TEST_TEXT", __v_7368.clone())?;
