let __v_7642 = pyrt::literals::decode("{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"chest infection\",\"chest infections\",\"a chest infection\",\"bronchitis\"]},\"Most chest infections clear in about a week to ten days, though the cough can hang on for three or four weeks afterwards. See a GP if you are breathless or coughing up blood, if the fever lasts more than five days, if it is getting worse rather than better after a week, or if you are over 65 or have a long-term chest condition, because those want treating sooner.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"covid\",\"coronavirus\",\"corona virus\"]},\"Most people are over the worst of covid in about a week, though a cough and tiredness commonly last two to four weeks and a lost sense of smell can take months to come back. Stay home while you have a temperature. Get help the same day if you are breathless, confused, or your lips or face look blue.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"sinus infection\",\"sinus infections\",\"sinusitis\",\"sinus\"]},\"Most sinus infections settle in two to three weeks without antibiotics: steam, a salt-water rinse and paracetamol, and give it ten days before expecting a turn. See a GP if it is worse after ten days, if it keeps coming back, or if one side of the face swells or the eye is affected, which wants seeing that day.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"pneumonia\"]},\"Most people with pneumonia start to feel better three to five days after treatment begins, and are back to normal in about six weeks, though tiredness can linger for months. Get seen the same day if breathing is fast or hard, the lips look blue, or you are confused.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"migraine\",\"migraines\",\"a headache\",\"headaches\",\"my headache\",\"head ache\",\"head aches\"]},\"A migraine attack usually runs from four hours to three days, and an ordinary headache from a few hours to a day or two. Get seen the same day for a headache that comes on like a thunderclap, one with a fever and a stiff neck, one after a bang on the head, or one with weakness, slurred speech or a change in vision.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"sickness bug\",\"sickness bugs\",\"stomach bug\",\"stomach bugs\",\"winter vomiting bug\",\"norovirus\",\"gastric flu\",\"tummy bug\"]},\"A sickness bug usually lasts one to three days, and you can feel washed out for a few days after that. You are most infectious in the 48 hours after it stops, so stay off work or school for two days after the last episode. Take small sips often; ring 111 if you cannot keep any fluid down, there is blood, or a baby is not wetting nappies.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"ear infection\",\"ear infections\",\"middle ear infection\"]},\"An ear infection usually settles in three to seven days without antibiotics. Give paracetamol or ibuprofen for the pain, and see a GP if there is discharge from the ear, if it is no better after three days, or the same day if there is swelling, redness or tenderness behind the ear.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"glue ear\",\"otitis media with effusion\",\"fluid in the ear\",\"fluid behind the eardrum\"]},\"Glue ear is fluid behind the eardrum rather than an infection, and it usually clears on its own but slowly: about half of children are clear within three months, and most within a year. Antibiotics and decongestants do not help it. Because the hearing is muffled while it lasts, ask for a hearing test if it has been there three months or more, and see a GP sooner if the child's speech is behind, if it keeps coming back, or if either ear is sore or running.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"inhaler\",\"inhalers\",\"blue inhaler\",\"brown inhaler\",\"ventolin\",\"salbutamol\",\"preventer inhaler\",\"reliever inhaler\",\"puffer\",\"puffs left\"]},\"A blue reliever inhaler holds 100 doses in the small canister and 200 in the bigger one, so at two puffs four times a day a 200-dose one lasts about three weeks, and one puff a day would stretch it to months. Most have a dose counter on the side now, and that number is what to go by rather than the date on the box. A brown preventer at two puffs twice a day runs out in about a month in the same way. Order the repeat before it empties rather than after, because the last puffs are weaker.\",{\"$tuple\":[\"side\",\"effect\",\"effects\",\"attack\",\"asthma\",\"wheeze\",\"wheezing\",\"expired\",\"expire\",\"breathless\",\"breathe\"]}]}]}")?;
