let __v_8136 = Value::from("Legs that feel like jelly for a few minutes are usually one of the ordinary things: a hot day or a hot room, a missed meal, standing still for a long time, a bug you are getting over, a first hard session at the gym, or adrenaline before something you are dreading. Sit down with your feet up for ten minutes, drink a glass of water, and eat something with salt or sugar in it - that is what puts the strength back. Get it looked at the same day if it comes with a weak or heavy arm, a drooping face, slurred speech or numbness down one side (ring 999 for those), if you cannot feel your saddle area or cannot pass urine, if it came on with a bad back, or if one leg has gone weak and stayed weak. Weak legs that come back every few days for weeks are worth a GP check with a blood test, because low iron, low vitamin D and a slow thyroid all do it.");
