let __v_8148 = Value::from("A churning or gurgling stomach is usually wind moving through a normal gut, and it is noisier when the gut is empty because there is only gas in there to move. Eat something plain if it has been hours - toast, rice, a banana - chew with your mouth closed, drink water rather than fizzy drinks, and take a ten minute walk, which shifts trapped wind better than anything. Butterflies before something nerve-racking are the same feeling and they pass. See a GP if it comes with pain that keeps coming back, blood in your poo, weight going down, a lump, or more than three weeks of it, and if you are vomiting or cannot keep fluids down, ring 111.");
