let __v_8648 = pyrt::literals::decode("{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"hernia\",{\"$tuple\":[\"hernia\",\"hernias\",\"inguinal hernia\",\"hiatus hernia\",\"hiatus hernias\",\"groin hernia\",\"stomach hernia\",\"umbilical hernia\",\"strangulated hernia\"]},\"A hernia is tissue pushing through a weak spot in the muscle wall: a soft lump in the groin or at the navel that shows when you cough or stand, and a hiatus hernia is the stomach sliding up into the chest and causing heartburn. Most are not urgent, and a GP refers the ones that hurt or keep growing for a small operation. Get it seen the same day if the lump goes hard, tender and will not push back in.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"carpal-tunnel\",{\"$tuple\":[\"carpal tunnel\",\"carpal tunnel syndrome\",\"tunnel in my wrist\",\"carpal\"]},\"Carpal tunnel is a nerve squeezed where it passes through the wrist: numbness, tingling or pins and needles in the thumb, index and middle fingers, often worst at night and eased by shaking the hand. A wrist splint worn at night from a pharmacy is the first thing and settles most mild cases; if the hand is weak or you keep dropping things, see a GP, because an injection or a small operation stops it getting worse.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"stomach-ulcer\",{\"$tuple\":[\"stomach ulcer\",\"stomach ulcers\",\"gastric ulcer\",\"duodenal ulcer\",\"peptic ulcer\",\"ulcer in my stomach\",\"ulcer in my tummy\",\"ulcers in my stomach\"]},\"A stomach ulcer is a raw patch in the lining of the stomach or the first part of the bowel, usually from an H. pylori infection or from ibuprofen and other anti-inflammatory painkillers: a gnawing or burning pain high in the belly, worse when you are hungry or at night. See a GP - a breath or stool test for H. pylori and a course of acid-suppressing tablets clears most of them. Ring 999 for vomited blood or black tarry stools.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"cellulitis\",{\"$tuple\":[\"cellulitis\",\"cellulitis infection\",\"skin infection cellulitis\"]},\"Cellulitis is a skin infection that turns an area red, hot, swollen and tender and keeps spreading, most often on a lower leg: it needs antibiotics the same day, so ring the GP or 111, and draw a line round the edge with a pen so you can see whether it is shrinking. Get seen urgently if it is on the face or near an eye, if the skin blisters or goes dark, or if there is a fever with shivering and feeling very unwell.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"long-covid\",{\"$tuple\":[\"long covid\",\"long-covid\",\"long covid symptoms\",\"post covid\",\"after covid\"]},\"Long covid is symptoms that carry on more than four weeks after the infection: breathlessness on the stairs, a tiredness that gets worse after effort, brain fog, a racing heart and poor sleep. What helps most is pacing - a small amount of activity, then a rest before you feel you need it, rather than pushing through - and a GP can refer you to a long covid clinic. Keep a note of what you did the day before a bad day.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"flu-jab\",{\"$tuple\":[\"flu jab\",\"flu jabs\",\"flu vaccine\",\"flu vaccines\",\"flu vaccination\",\"flu shot\",\"flu injection\",\"jab for flu\",\"vaccine for flu\",\"the flu jab\",\"the flu vaccine\"]},\"The flu jab is one injection in the arm, best in October, and it is free on the NHS for anyone over 65, pregnant women, children from 2 up to 17 as a nasal spray, carers, and people with asthma, diabetes, heart, lung or kidney disease or a weakened immune system. It cannot give you flu; a sore arm for a day or two is the usual reaction. A pharmacy or the GP surgery books it.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"blood-clot\",{\"$tuple\":[\"dvt\",\"deep vein thrombosis\",\"blood clot\",\"blood clots\",\"clot in my leg\",\"blood clot in my leg\",\"clot in the leg\",\"thrombosis\"]},\"A DVT is a clot in a deep vein, usually in the calf: one leg swollen, warm and tender, often with a heavy ache, and it is a same-day job - ring 111 or the GP, because a clot can travel to the lung. Sudden breathlessness, a sharp pain when you breathe in, or coughing blood means a clot may already be there, so ring 999. The GP sorts the scan and the blood thinner; do not rub the leg or wait to see if it settles.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"scarlet-fever\",{\"$tuple\":[\"scarlet fever\",\"scarletina\",\"strawberry tongue\",\"sandpaper rash\"]},\"Scarlet fever is a strep infection: a sore throat with a rough, sandpapery rash that feels like goosebumps, flushed cheeks and a red strawberry tongue, and it needs antibiotics from a GP the same day - children are usually much better within 24 to 48 hours of starting them. Keep them off school until 24 hours of antibiotics have been taken, give plenty to drink and paracetamol for the sore throat, and get advice if the fever lasts past five days, the rash spreads, or there is earache or swelling in the neck.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"dengue\",{\"$tuple\":[\"dengue\",\"dengue fever\",\"breakbone fever\"]},\"Dengue is a virus spread by daytime-biting mosquitoes in the tropics, and it is not passed from person to person: sudden high fever, a severe headache behind the eyes, deep muscle and joint pain and often a rash, with the fever usually breaking after three to seven days. Take paracetamol only - ibuprofen and aspirin raise the risk of bleeding - drink plenty, and get seen the same day for sickness that will not stop, tummy pain, bleeding gums or nose, or drowsiness, because those are the warning signs of the severe form. It is worth telling any doctor you see where you travelled.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"yellow-fever\",{\"$tuple\":[\"yellow fever\",\"yellow fever vaccine\",\"yellow fever jab\"]},\"Yellow fever is a mosquito-borne virus in parts of Africa and South America, and most people have a fever, headache, muscle ache and sickness for about a week and then recover. A small share go on to jaundice, bleeding and organ failure, which is a 999 emergency, so get seen quickly for yellow skin or eyes, bleeding or vomiting. The vaccine is the protection: a travel clinic gives it, some countries require a certificate to enter, and it needs booking at least six to eight weeks before you fly.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[\"rheumatic-fever\",{\"$tuple\":[\"rheumatic fever\",\"rheumatic\",\"strep throat\",\"strep a\"]},\"Rheumatic fever is the body reacting to an untreated strep throat or scarlet fever two to four weeks later: a fever with painful, swollen joints that move around, sometimes a rash and a racing heart, and it needs a GP the same day because it can scar the heart valves. The protection is treating a sore throat with the antibiotics the GP prescribes and finishing the course, so a sore throat with a fever and swollen neck glands in a child is worth having swabbed rather than waited out. It is now rare in the UK but still seen in children aged 5 to 15.\"]}]}")?;
