let __v_9055 = Value::from("A hernia is a piece of bowel or fat pushing out through a weak spot in the wall of muscle that is meant to hold it in - commonest in the groin, where the wall is thin already, and then at the belly button or along an old operation scar. It shows as a soft lump that is there when you stand and cough and gone when you lie down, and it is usually a dull ache rather than a pain. It will not mend itself, and it does not need a repair unless it is bothering you, but it does need to be looked at by a GP so the diagnosis is on your record. A hiatus hernia is different: the top of the stomach slides up through the diaphragm into the chest, which causes heartburn and is treated with the reflux advice and a tablet rather than an operation. Go to A&E the same day if a lump that used to go back in becomes hard and very tender, or comes with vomiting, a swollen belly or no wind - that is a hernia that has been trapped, and it needs a surgeon rather than a wait.");
